<title>NEW ZEALAND: Treasury sees NZ inflation at 2.1 pct in 97.</title>
<headline>Treasury sees NZ inflation at 2.1 pct in 97.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-12-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Treasury on Monday forecast New Zealand underlying inflation would be at 2.1 percent in the March 1997 year.</p>
<p>The following is a table of forecasts from Treasury's December Economic and Fiscal Update with previous forecasts from the September pre-election forecasts in brackets (percentages unless otherwise stated:</p>
<p>		 1996/97	1997/98	1998/99	1999/00</p>
<p>Inflation    2.1 (2.1)    1.2 (1.4)    1.5 (1.0)    1.2 (1.0)</p>
<p>90 day bills 9.3 (9.3)    8.0 (8.0)    7.3 (7.5)    6.3 (6.5)</p>
<p>10-yr bonds  7.8 (8.0)    6.7 (7.1)    6.6 (7.0)    6.4 (6.5)</p>
</text>
